And as I already said on the top post, this audio, once it's been pulled
apart into a usable format (the goal of this project), it will be the audio
for the various learning programs currently in existence and probably for
future ones as well. This means the current lessons on Anki and Memrise
specifically, and more generally any other places where someone feels
inclined to upload audio for how to pronounce the gismu.

That's why the thread is named "Gismu audio crowd source project": because
it is a Project, which is being Crowd Sourced, to complete work on the
Audio for the Gismu.

